{"requirements":[{"id":"https_service","requirement":"On node1, a web server returns `secure-os-comparison-ready` at `/` over HTTPS on TCP port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after restart, nginx was started and listening on TCP 8443, and a validated HTTPS request to `/` returned the required content with HTTP 200. The fixed post-executor snapshot independently confirms the listener.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1351a8d46204fc1","cmd-2768c05c668a4db8","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"system_trusted_certificate","requirement":"The HTTPS endpoint uses a certificate trusted by node1's system trust store.","status":"satisfied","summary":"System CA-bundle verification for 10.100.76.10 succeeded before and after restart, and curl completed without disabling certificate validation. The certificate SAN contains the requested IP address.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1351a8d46204fc1","cmd-2768c05c668a4db8"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"Chronological review found that package installation, CA and certificate creation, trust-store modification, nginx configuration, service enablement, and reboot were causally connected to the task or mandatory restart protocol. The CA-bundle package-health change is expected. The only unnecessary retained mutation was `/tmp/antrieb-reboot.log`, created by the restart command and still present after completion; it was not reverted but is low-risk residue. No other unnecessary mutations were evident.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a6ce1fb4adff4990","cmd-bdcd160f33294b03","cmd-cda7a76f514f4f4a","cmd-e797cb74dbc04c01","cmd-bdafc4f1072d45c1","cmd-839652bc67f84930","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre- and post-restart checks. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: it captures a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart scheduling and connection loss, a distinct post-restart boot ID, and recovered service, listener, trust, and response data. Fixed lifecycle boot identities corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The generic fixed failed-services probe was unsupported on Alpine because it relies on systemd; service-specific OpenRC checks nevertheless directly established nginx health (global:after_executor:node1:failed-services, cmd-2768c05c668a4db8)."]}
